{
  "id": "m40l1",
  "title": {
    "es": "Mezcla y mergesort",
    "en": "Merge and mergesort"
  },
  "theory": {
    "es": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Dividir y vencer"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "**Mergesort** divide la lista en mitades, ordena cada mitad (recursivamente) y luego **mezcla** las dos mitades ordenadas. Mezclar dos listas ya ordenadas es fácil y rápido."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "def mezclar(a, b):",
          "    r, i, j = [], 0, 0",
          "    while i < len(a) and j < len(b):",
          "        if a[i] <= b[j]:",
          "            r.append(a[i]); i += 1",
          "        else:",
          "            r.append(b[j]); j += 1",
          "    return r + a[i:] + b[j:]",
          "",
          "print(mezclar([1, 3], [2, 4]))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "[1, 2, 3, 4]"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Mergesort es O(n log n): muchísimo mejor que burbuja para listas grandes."
      }
    ],
    "en": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Divide and conquer"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "**Mergesort** splits the list into halves, sorts each half (recursively) and then **merges** the two sorted halves. Merging two already-sorted lists is easy and fast."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "def mezclar(a, b):",
          "    r, i, j = [], 0, 0",
          "    while i < len(a) and j < len(b):",
          "        if a[i] <= b[j]:",
          "            r.append(a[i]); i += 1",
          "        else:",
          "            r.append(b[j]); j += 1",
          "    return r + a[i:] + b[j:]",
          "",
          "print(mezclar([1, 3], [2, 4]))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "[1, 2, 3, 4]"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Mergesort is O(n log n): far better than bubble sort for large lists."
      }
    ]
  },
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "m40l1e1",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `mezclar(a, b)` que combine dos listas YA ORDENADAS en una sola lista ordenada.",
        "en": "Define `mezclar(a, b)` combining two ALREADY-SORTED lists into one sorted list."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "def mezclar(a, b):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "def mezclar(a, b):",
        "    r, i, j = [], 0, 0",
        "    while i < len(a) and j < len(b):",
        "        if a[i] <= b[j]:",
        "            r.append(a[i]); i += 1",
        "        else:",
        "            r.append(b[j]); j += 1",
        "    return r + a[i:] + b[j:]"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "Avanza dos índices comparando, y añade el resto al final."
        ],
        "en": [
          "Advance two indices comparing, then append the rest."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
